      "color": "orange",
      "text": "Trading Desk. A broker terminal: dense panes on 1-px seams, condensed numerals, the option as an order ticket.\n\nLayout: Full-bleed pane grid (watchlist, chart, ticket) with tabbed pane headers; compact rows; nothing floats.\nThe memorable thing: The option ticket beside the candles: market close against the model price, one tap to price.\nType: Barlow Condensed 600 for prices and headings (numbers fit dense panes); Barlow 400–700 for text.\nLight: bg #E6E9ED, surf #FFFFFF, ink #14171A, muted #59616D, acc #5A3FE6, line #D5DAE0\nDark: bg #0B0E11, surf #12161B, ink #EAECEF, muted #8A94A2, acc #9B87FF, line #262D36\nMagnet rail on the left edge. Live prices on these boards are NSE closing prices from 25 Sep 2026; every chart is drawn from real data or the project's pricer."
    }
